## What is wrong (one paragraph)

`POST /api/documents/:id/sign-cert` refuses a `metadata.documentType` that differs from the source type at `:2590`
(`metadata.documentType !== undefined && metadata.documentType !== source.type`). When the source row carries **no `type` at all**,
`source.type` is `undefined`, the second clause is still true for any named type, and the request is correctly refused 400. Nothing
in the suite pins that. The #1031 gate measured it directly (section 4, row Q-SIGNCERT-UNTYPED-SOURCE-SKIP): prefixing the guard with
`typeof source.type === 'string' &&` - so an untyped source SKIPS the guard - gives **0 reds on 64 / 741**, while the probe C-D02
(untyped source + `DEGREE`) turns from 400 into **201, stored type absent, served DEGREE, sign upstream 1**. **This task:** a new
`describe` block with two cells - RED (an untyped source is still refused) and a CONTROL (a typed source is still refused a differing
relabel, which stays green under the tamper because its `source.type` IS a string). No product line changes.

## Where (no product site changes - this list is informational; every line below STAYS)

