Red under the tamper: U1 fails at `.toEqual` by assertion. With `typeof source.type === 'string' &&` prefixed, an untyped source makes
the guard false, the handler signs and saves, and U1 reads `{ status: 201, code: null, saved: 1, stored: null, served: 'DEGREE' }`
instead of `REFUSED` (`stored` is `null` because `saveDocument` round-trips the record through `JSON.stringify`, which drops an
`undefined` `type`; `served` is `data.documentType || type` = `DEGREE`). Green at the tip: `source.type` is `undefined`,
`'DEGREE' !== undefined` is true, and the guard returns 400 before any upstream call. The CONTROL is green on BOTH trees: its source
type is the string `'DOCUMENT'`, so `typeof source.type === 'string'` is true and the guard evaluates exactly as it does at the tip,
refusing `PROPERTY_DEED` 400. Every existing cell stays green on both trees - the tamper is pinned to line 2590, which is the
sign-cert guard only, and every existing sign-cert cell seeds a STRING-typed source.

